The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This route adds CED online audio decoding/staging, explicit training
audits, eight-GPU microbatch-eight with four-step gradient accumulation,
and complete-state checkpoints.
Reference source file identities are recorded in reference_audit.json.

The loader, mapping and audio recipe derive from the isolated two-loop
layer4/8 input-reinjection Loop-LoRA route. This isolated copy executes the
pure text model's three-loop schedule with three independent LoRA sets.
CED intermediate injection remains limited to the first two loops.
The shared text model and original audio routes are unchanged.
source_guard.json protects their identities; parent_reference_audit.json
retains the parent route's historical audit.
